    },
    "body": "Before: exports could show a different number from the issued report. SIS v1, the adapter, the v1 matrix and GeoJSON, the WET_CHEM and SPECTRAL exports and the data-results grid each picked their own value; SPECTRAL read raw results directly.\n\nAfter: every export and the grid show the saved reported value as the headline. It equals the report item's unrounded value, in the analysis's own unit. Each flat export also names where the value came from: `<p>_selection_id`, `<p>_attempt_ids` and `<p>_batch_ids`. The results CSV and XLSX add the selection, attempt and batch ids to each row.\n\nNormalized values still appear, but only in the `_normalized` columns.\n\n**SIS v2 stays the raw-observation contract.** It still serves raw observations, not reported values. The only change is two new nullable fields on each observation, `attemptId` and `batchId`, declared in the v2 capabilities. Source observations, cursors and counts are unchanged.\n\n**Out of scope here:** the report's own basis, rounding and revision numbering stay as #211 and #212 shipped them. This PR changes only what the exports read; it does not touch how reports are built. The stored-unit, censoring and ambiguity guards from f830 are kept as they are.\n\nHow: `reportedValueReadService` now returns per-value batch ids. The export controllers and `sisAdapterService` read from it instead of from raw results. `issue_213_export_equals_report.test.js` checks that the export equals the report for each path. The help release manifest is regenerated for the three new translation keys.\n\nChecks at 990a4cb5, rebased on main f830f900:\n- `issue_213_export_equals_report`, `export_normalization` and `sis_adapter_service` pass, 27 of 27 tests.\n- The 17 server suites that touch the changed files pass, 247 of 247 tests.\n- Client build passes, and lint shows 0 errors and 14 warnings.\n- The full server suite is running on this head.\n\nRefs #213. The audit-gate convention is that #213 closes only after the post-deploy check, so this PR deliberately says Refs rather than Closes.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01869phMNBbSrZkcCR7UBe9J",
